{"schemaVersion":1,"generatedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","id":"d7850396aab66b71c6abe5fb","canonicalUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260813030515.1028627-1-twoerner%40gmail.com/","channels":["openembedded-core"],"thread":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"thread:lore-git:20260813030515.1028627-1-twoerner@gmail.com","source":{"kind":"static-generated","canonicalThreadUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260813030515.1028627-1-twoerner%40gmail.com/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","contentDigest":"lore-git:20260813030515.1028627-1-twoerner@gmail.com"},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v2 1/2] oeqa/sdk: update cryptodev to a revision that builds on kernel 6.18","messages":{"7fc0bf78c8046ad9c23e49f80d8ed93103db3317.camel@pbarker.dev":{"id":"7fc0bf78c8046ad9c23e49f80d8ed93103db3317.camel@pbarker.dev","messageId":"7fc0bf78c8046ad9c23e49f80d8ed93103db3317.camel@pbarker.dev","references":["20260813030515.1028627-1-twoerner@gmail.com","20260813030515.1028627-2-twoerner@gmail.com"],"missingAncestorIds":["20260813030515.1028627-2-twoerner@gmail.com","20260813030515.1028627-1-twoerner@gmail.com"],"author":{"name":"Paul Barker","address":"paul@pbarker.dev"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Trevor Woerner","address":"twoerner@gmail.com"},{"name":"","address":"openembedded-core@lists.openembedded.org"}],"cc":[],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-16T11:12:49.000Z","iso":"2026-08-16T11:12:49.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v2 1/2] oeqa/sdk: update cryptodev to a revision that builds on kernel 6.18","mailingLists":[{"id":"openembedded-core.lists.openembedded.org","displayName":"openembedded-core.lists.openembedded.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"quote","attribution":"On Wed, 2026-08-12 at 23:05 -0400, Trevor Woerner wrote:","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"The out-of-tree kernel module test pins a cryptodev-linux revision from"},{"depth":1,"text":"before the 1.14 release, which predates the removal of"},{"depth":1,"text":"crypto_ahash_alignmask() from the kernel and so no longer compiles:"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"  cryptlib.c:384:28: error: implicit declaration of function"},{"depth":1,"text":"  'crypto_ahash_alignmask' [-Wimplicit-function-declaration]"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Move to upstream's \"Fix build for Linux 6.18-rc1\", which is the revision"},{"depth":1,"text":"that restores compatibility."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"AI-Generated: codex/claude-opus 5 (xhigh)"},{"depth":1,"text":"Signed-off-by: Trevor Woerner <twoerner@gmail.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"---"},{"depth":1,"text":"changes in v2:"},{"depth":1,"text":"- none"},{"depth":1,"text":"---"},{"depth":1,"text":" meta/lib/oeqa/sdk/cases/kmod.py | 4 ++--"},{"depth":1,"text":" 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"diff --git a/meta/lib/oeqa/sdk/cases/kmod.py b/meta/lib/oeqa/sdk/cases/kmod.py"},{"depth":1,"text":"index 0c4d8ddb543f..1be23e994fd2 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"--- a/meta/lib/oeqa/sdk/cases/kmod.py"},{"depth":1,"text":"+++ b/meta/lib/oeqa/sdk/cases/kmod.py"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -31,8 +31,8 @@ class KernelModuleTest(OESDKTestCase):"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":"         with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix=\"cryptodev\", dir=self.tc.sdk_dir) as testdir:"},{"depth":1,"text":"             git_url = \"https://github.com/cryptodev-linux/cryptodev-linux\""},{"depth":1,"text":"-            # This is a knnown-good commit post-1.13 that builds with kernel 6.7+"},{"depth":1,"text":"-            git_sha = \"bb8bc7cf60d2c0b097c8b3b0e807f805b577a53f\""},{"depth":1,"text":"+            # This is a known-good commit post-1.14 that builds with kernel 6.18+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+            git_sha = \"08644db02d43478f802755903212f5ee506af73b\""},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":"             sourcedir = os.path.join(testdir, \"cryptodev-linux\")"},{"depth":1,"text":"             subprocess.check_output([\"git\", \"clone\", git_url, sourcedir], stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)"}],"lineCount":34,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Hi Trevor,"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"I'm wondering why we haven't spotted this issue previously, we've been\nusing Linux 6.18 for months now. Are we missing a test case?"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Best regards,"},{"kind":"signature","text":"Paul Barker","lineCount":1}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":0,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260813030515.1028627-2-twoerner@gmail.com"}},"rootIds":["7fc0bf78c8046ad9c23e49f80d8ed93103db3317.camel@pbarker.dev"],"childrenByParent":{},"chronologicalIds":["7fc0bf78c8046ad9c23e49f80d8ed93103db3317.camel@pbarker.dev"],"patchSeries":[],"diagnostics":[],"patches":{}}}